      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:107:4",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) كُلَّمَا ازْدَادَ الْعَبْدُ إِيمَاناً ازْدَادَ ضِيقاً فِي مَعِيشَتِهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "From him, from Muhammad Bin Ali, from Dawood Al Haza’a, from Muhammad Bin Sagheer, from his grandfather Shuayb, from Mufazzal who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Every time the <span class=\"iTxt\">Emān</span> of the servant increases, the constriction in his livelihood increases’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. It is narrated from him (narrator of the Hadith above) from Muhammad ibn Ali from Dawud al-Hadhdha’ from Muhammad ibn Saghir from his grandfather, Shu’ayb from Mufaddal who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) has said, ‘As the belief of a person increases in strength, his poverty intensifies.’” "
        ]
      }
